---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy"
            description="Privacy policy for WPReadme Preview. Your readme.txt content is processed entirely in your browser and never leaves your device."
            current="privacy">
    <section class="page-hero">
        <div class="container">
            <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="page-subtitle">
                WPReadme Preview is designed to respect your privacy. This policy explains what
                happens to data when you use wpreadme.ir.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container content">
        <h2>Readme content stays in your browser</h2>
        <p>
            The readme.txt text you paste or upload is processed entirely in your browser with JavaScript.
            It is never sent to, stored on, or logged by our servers. When you close the tab, the content
            is discarded; nothing about your plugin is retained between visits.
        </p>

        <h2>Local storage</h2>
        <p>
            We store a single preference key (your light/dark theme choice) in your browser's local
            storage so the site remembers how you like it displayed. It never leaves your device, and you
            can clear it at any time through your browser settings without affecting functionality.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
            We use Google Tag Manager to collect anonymous usage statistics such as page views, referrers,
            and approximate location. These analytics may set cookies on your device. You can block them
            with any ad blocker or browser setting, and every feature of this tool keeps working.
        </p>

        <h2>No accounts, no data sales</h2>
        <p>
            There is no registration and no login, so we have no user database. Because we do not collect
            personal information, we never sell or share personal data with anyone.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party pages</h2>
        <p>
            This site links to third-party websites such as the WordPress.org developer documentation and
            social profiles. We are not responsible for their content or privacy practices.
        </p>

        <h2>Donations</h2>
        <p>
            Donations are handled on public blockchain networks such as Bitcoin and Ethereum. Transactions
            are pseudonymous and permanently visible on the respective ledgers. We cannot link a
            transaction to your identity unless you choose to tell us who you are.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>
            Material changes to this policy will be published on this page with an updated date. For
            privacy questions or data removal requests, email parsadeng@gmail.com or reach the developer
            through any channel listed on the contact page and mention privacy in your message.
        </p>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .page-hero {
        background: var(--primary);
        padding: 5rem 0 3.5rem;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .page-title {
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        color: #fff;
    }

    .page-subtitle {
        color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
        max-width: 42rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .content {
        max-width: 52rem;
        padding-bottom: 5rem;
    }

    .content h2 {
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        margin: 2.5rem 0 0.8rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .content h2:first-of-type {
        margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .content p {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        line-height: 1.75;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .content a:not(.btn) {
        color: #5b8def;
    }
</style>
